From: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:15:00 +0100
Subject: arm64: dts: rockchip: rock-2f: Limit PCIe to Gen1

Gen2 is not reliable on the PCIe FPC connector with an adapter board.
Link training reaches Gen2 only sometimes. A speed change to Gen2 takes
the link down. Seen with an RX 550: its SMU starts a speed change during
amdgpu init.

Limit the link to Gen1. amdgpu reads the root port capability, so it
also stays at Gen1.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2f.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2f.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2f.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2f.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2f.dts
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 };
 
 &pcie {
+	max-link-speed = <1>;
 	reset-gpios = <&gpio1 RK_PA2 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 	vpcie3v3-supply = <&vcc3v3_pcie20>;
 	status = "okay";
-- 
Armbian

